# fixedbugs, defect 439, lane b14-resolve, 2026-10-07, found beside defect
# 401 by lane b13-zero401.
#
# SYMPTOM: an `@` handed to a call whose callee is a name nothing binds, or a
# variant named as a value, kept its mark, so a name bound with `=` was told
# `not_mutable` beside `unknown_name` or `variant_in_value_position`: a
# second message for one mistake, and a repair nobody can know is owed until
# the callee is known (`bmup(@n)` is told nothing about `n` now, whether the
# function it meant takes an `@` or not).
#
# CAUSE: the name stage held an `@` to the rule of the left of `@` before
# anything knew whether the call writes the argument back.
#
# FIX: the mark stays only on an argument whose parameter, at its position,
# takes an `@`; a callee that resolved to nothing, a module or a variant has
# none, so the `@` is set aside untold and the callee's own mistake is the one
# message.

variant Mode
    on
    off

function bump(@x: i64)
    x @ x + 1

function main()
    n = 1
    m = 2
    bmup(@n)  #~ unknown_name
    grow(@n, k: @m)  #~ unknown_name
    print(Mode(@n))  #~ variant_in_value_position
    print(n + m)
